  "reason": "Evidence: The current best model (config_006, rna_only/multiprofile/scvi_n200/transformer) achieves 0.653 acc, while image-only with resnet50 (config_010) is at 0.208—essentially random. This creates a critical uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative for this task, or is resnet50 simply too weak an encoder to extract useful features? Question: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_010, swapping only the image encoder to a much stronger pretrained ViT-L. It directly tests whether the image modality carries any predictive signal with a capable encoder. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing in any of the 24+ multimodal fusion configurations, I need to know whether image features can contribute meaningfully at all. If ViT-L image-only remains near-random, multimodal fusion is unlikely to help and I should focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinements. If it shows a meaningful signal (e.g., >0.40), then multimodal experiments become well-justified and I can prioritize them. This single experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty in the search space and guides all subsequent decisions."
}

